---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { LINKS, SITE } from "../config/links";
const updated = "October 19, 2026";
---
<Base title="Privacy policy · InnerBoard IOS" description="What this site collects, and what it does with it. This policy covers innerboardos.com. We do not sell personal information. We do not show advertising." path="/privacy" theme="cream" navStart="light">
  <article class="wrap prose-ib io-legal">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p>
    <h1 class="t-m">What this site collects, and what it does with it.</h1>
    <p class="t-cap io-legal-date">Last updated {updated}. This policy covers innerboardos.com. Practice by InnerBoard, the app, has its own policy inside the app.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>This site is a set of pages. It does not ask you to create an account and it does not sell anything directly. When you visit, our hosting provider records the standard technical details every web server sees: your IP address, browser, the pages you open and the time you opened them. We use these to keep the site running and to understand which pages people read.</p>
    <p>If analytics is enabled on this site, it records which buttons are pressed (for example, that somebody opened the assessment or asked to talk to our team) so we can see what is useful. These events carry no name or email address.</p>

    <h2>Campaign links</h2>
    <p>Links that bring you here from an email, a post or a partner may carry campaign parameters. When you continue to the Company OS Score or the app, those parameters travel with you so the score can be counted under the campaign that brought you. They identify the campaign, not you.</p>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <p>We do not sell personal information. We do not show advertising. We do not use tracking that follows you to other websites.</p>

    <h2>When you contact us</h2>
    <p>If you email us or book a conversation, we keep what you send so we can reply and so the conversation has a record. We do not add you to any list you did not ask to join.</p>

    <h2>The assessment and the app</h2>
    <p>The Company OS Score runs inside Practice by InnerBoard. Its handling of your answers, and the account you may choose to create there, are covered by the app's own privacy policy and terms, which you can read inside the app.</p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>You can read this site without accepting anything. To ask what we hold about you, to correct it, or to have it deleted, write to <a href={`mailto:${LINKS.contactEmail}`}>{LINKS.contactEmail}</a>.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it.</p>
    <p class="t-cap io-legal-note">{SITE.name} is operated by InnerBoard. This policy is written in plain language and should be reviewed by counsel before launch.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
<style>
  /* The legal page (IOS_SPEC 2.12): the system's prose rules; only the column and its padding are set here. */
  .io-legal { max-width: 40em; padding-top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 64px); padding-bottom: var(--sec); }
  .io-legal h1 { margin-top: 0; }
  /* The date line and the closing note at 14 px (audit 2, P2 21). */
  .io-legal p.t-cap { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--fg-3); }
  /* The eyebrow keeps its own size and colour against the prose paragraph rule. */
  .io-legal p.eyebrow { margin-top: 0; font-size: var(--fs-eyebrow); line-height: 1; color: var(--fg-3); }
  .io-legal-date { margin-top: 12px; }
  .io-legal-note { margin-top: 28px; }
</style>
